  "row_count": "rowbands.py: p5 geometry ok, 25 bands, data bands start at 16.52% on a 1.585% pitch - 19 data bands, 19 rows emitted; p8 ok, 13 bands, 5 data bands from 17.75%, 5 rows emitted. p6 and p9 return no-reliable-geometry for horizontal rules at 200/300/400 dpi (the attachment's inner rules are too faint), so those two were scored by an INDEPENDENT ink-profile of the amount column instead: p6 yields exactly 20 inked data bands plus one TOTAL band, p9 exactly 7 plus one TOTAL band, matching the 20 and 7 rows emitted. The same ink profile independently reproduces the 19 and 5 counts on p5 and p8 and locates the TOTAL / more-than-$50 / less-than-$50 bands in their expected places.",
