 "notes": "BUNDLE of 3 reports, OUT OF CHRONOLOGICAL ORDER - the PDF opens with the 2015-01-05 annual report (report 1), then the 2014-04-03 pre-convention report (report 2), then the 2014-06-10 pre-primary report (report 3). n_reports_in_pdf 3 agrees with the chunk file. All three covers are Generation 1 (Carr Printing 5-5-PG). Reports 2 and 3 DO NOT use the printed Form A/Form B sheets at all: the filer substituted his own typed spreadsheet ('ITEMIZED CONTRIBUTION REPORT - FORM A' / '- FORM B') which carries its own TOTAL and, on Form A, its own 'more than $50.00' and 'less than $50.00' subtotal lines - a real second anchor that a Gen-1 filing does not normally have. The schedules are NOT photocopied across reports: each report carries its own distinct, non-overlapping date range. index.csv says candidate 'THOMAS WESLY DURRANT', office 'Assessor' - all three covers agree ('Full Name of Candidate THOMAS WESLY DURRANT', 'Name of Office COUNTY ASSESSOR', party REPUBLICAN); no contradiction. Clerk RECEIVED stamps: JAN 5 2015 (report 1), APR 4 2014 (report 2), JUN 10 2014 (report 3). Candidate home address, ZIP and both phone numbers appear in the clear on all three covers and were discarded at read time. Donor street addresses and ZIPs on the attachments were likewise discarded; only city and state are retained. The five dated-but-unnamed lines on report 2's Form A (and the one on report 3's) are the filer's own itemisation of his sub-$50 aggregate - they are real printed lines and are emitted with an honestly blank donor, NOT dropped; a human may wish to decide whether an unnamed sub-$50 line belongs in the itemized layer. Page rot 270; poppler renders all nine pages upright portrait 1700x2200.",
